+# Sequence-parallel namespace fallback and PCIe benchmark syntax cleanup
+
+BUG-009 gives normal parser results a disabled `sequence_parallel` field and makes the optimizer treat legacy Namespaces without it as disabled, eliminating the TP>1 replay crash without adding a standard CLI switch. Explicit `True` still reaches the pre-existing LayerNorm-gradient reduction only when an external/custom caller supplies it, preserving compatibility without claiming feature support. BUG-010 removes the exact invalid pseudocode tail appended to the PCIe benchmark and restores whole-tree parsing without changing benchmark behavior. Tests, records, index, and worktree agree; the only **confirmed, non-blocking** gap is target GPU replay evidence.
+
+**Blocking findings:** none. **Non-blocking findings:** one—BUG-009 needs the documented TP/NCCL replay run before its status can advance.
+
+Watch for: **confirmed, non-blocking** — CPU/AST tests prove the missing-field and branch contracts, but no repaired 8→7 GPU replay has shown iteration 3 crossing optimizer reduction and reaching iteration 4.
+
+**Review result**: PASS
+
+**Verdict**: APPROVED
+
+## High-level view
+
+The parser creates a hidden `False` schema field rather than registering `--sequence-parallel`. The optimizer fallback gives absent fields the same disabled behavior, while explicit `True` keeps the old TP>1 branch available only across the external compatibility boundary.
+
+The AST suite exercises source definitions without importing Torch or Apex. A skip-path sentinel proves genuine short-circuiting, and the TP2/`True` case checks both TP-group all-reduce and gradient-buffer writeback.
+
+The PCIe change deletes a historically isolated, unparseable draft with no callers; the real layer-change dynamic programming remains in `delta_space_dp()`. BUG-010's `已验证` status is syntax-scoped, while BUG-009 correctly remains `修复已实施，待验证` because the **confirmed, non-blocking** GPU evidence gap remains.
+
+<details>
+<summary>Issues (1)</summary>
+
+1. **Target TP replay evidence pending (non-blocking, confirmed)** — Local contracts cannot prove the repaired 8→7 TP/Apex/NCCL replay crosses optimizer reduction. Run the documented remote acceptance scenario before advancing BUG-009 to `已验证`.
+
+</details>
+
+<details>
+<summary>Details</summary>
+
+## Disabled schema with a narrow legacy `True` boundary
+
+`parser.set_defaults(sequence_parallel=False)` creates no argument action: the standard parser rejects `--sequence-parallel`, and repository search finds no other argument, config loader, model path, or parameter-marking producer. The later `parse_args(defaults=...)` loop only replaces `None`, so that API cannot turn the hidden `False` into `True`.
+
+`getattr(args, 'sequence_parallel', False)` changes only the missing-field case. Missing and explicit `False` skip model inspection and collectives for TP1 and TP2; TP1 short-circuits externally supplied `True`; TP2 plus explicit `True` retains the prior marked-parameter reduction. A custom argument provider or hand-built Namespace can still supply `True`, but that pre-existing boundary remains unsupported.
+
+The split avoids exposing an option without model/dataflow support while preserving external callers that already provide the full legacy contract.
+
+## AST contracts distinguish fallback, short-circuit, and reduction
+
+The test parses each complete source file and compiles only `_add_distributed_args()` or `MegatronOptimizer.allreduce_layernorm_grads()`, remaining CPU-only while still catching source syntax and target-definition failures. The parser assertion proves the field is present and identically `False`.
+
+Five skip combinations cover missing at TP1/TP2, `False` at TP1/TP2, and `True` at TP1. `_NeverIterate` fails if any skip case inspects models. The TP2/`True` case supplies a marked parameter and verifies TP-group all-reduce followed by buffer copyback, directly exercising the retained branch.
+
+## Historical tail removal restores only the parser contract
+
+History attributes the 27-line tail to a later cleanup commit rather than the original benchmark. Empty assignments, bare English, a function-external `return`, undefined dependencies, and a non-progressing loop make it neither parsable nor salvageable as a standalone helper; repository search finds no `getT()` caller. Removal restores the original benchmark apart from one EOF blank line, while `aceso/elaceso_dp.py::delta_space_dp()` remains the executable related implementation.
+
+Compilation proves BUG-010's syntax defect is repaired. The record does not claim CUDA transfer correctness, import safety, memory safety, or performance validation, so `已验证` stays within the evidence.
+
+## Records and validation match the reviewed worktree
+
+BUG-009 preserves the first `AttributeError`, separates the BUG-002 recovery cascade, lists both production changes and the AST test, and requires a fresh GPU run before advancing status. BUG-010 records its independent compile failure, historical source, exact deletion scope, and syntax-only validation. Index IDs, titles, statuses, dates, filenames, and cross-links match.
+
+**Confirmed, non-blocking:** no post-fix TP2/Apex/NCCL run exists. Complete the documented remote acceptance run before changing BUG-009 to `已验证`; any later failure beyond this attribute access needs separate root-cause handling.
+
+Validation rerun during review:
